/* book exam traps: Saying a quantum dot changes colour because it is bigger and scatters more light. The cause is quantum confinement of the electron and hole, which raises the band gap as the dot shrinks. | Treating FRET efficiency as linear in distance. E falls with the sixth power of r, so small distance changes give large signal changes. | Reversing the gold colours: dispersed 20–40 nm gold is red; aggregated gold is blue-purple. | Forgetting Debye screening: a nanowire or graphene FET in undiluted serum detects only charge within about 1 nm of the surface, not every bound molecule. | Confusing Förster radius R0 with the particle radius. R0 is the donor–acceptor distance where FRET efficiency is 0.5. */
